 "notes": "Libretto by Lorenzo Da Ponte (1787). Words follow the Schirmer vocal score's spelling and punctuation (cangierò; d'un' with the print's apostrophe in bars 54 and 62). In bars 23 and 42 the print has \"tuo sorte\" where the libretto has \"tua sorte\"; the words follow the print, and singers normally sing tua (IPA ˈtu.a). Zerlina sings vor-re-i and sa-re-i on three notes where the line has them on three syllables, vor-rei on two in bars 8-9 and 31-32. IPA, word meanings and translations were drafted for this app (S14) and the IPA was checked against Castel. IPA follows sung Italian conventions: stressed syllable marked, elisions (two words on one note in the score) joined with ‿, open e/o as ɛ/ɔ. Translation literal, for meaning.",
